>
  <DetailSection title="Overview">
    <p class="placeholder">
      What the application does, how many people were in the group, and how
      long you had.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection title="My contribution">
    <p class="placeholder">
      Which parts you personally wrote. Be specific and be honest — this is
      the section that does the work now the source is not public, and it is
      the first thing an interviewer will ask you to expand on.
    </p>
    <p class="placeholder">
      If you led on a design decision or unblocked someone else, say so.
      Working well in a group is a large part of what this project shows.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection title="How it works">
    <p class="placeholder">
      The interesting decision here is choosing transport per data type:
      TCP for messages and file transfer where you cannot lose anything, UDP
      for webcam frames where a dropped frame matters less than a late one.
      Explain that tradeoff properly — it is the strongest technical idea in
      the project.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection title="Problems I hit">
    <p class="placeholder">
      Frame reassembly, packet ordering, concurrency, dropped connections —
      whichever ones you actually wrestled with, and what you did about
      them.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>

  <DetailSection title="What I learned">
    <p class="placeholder">
      What you took away, technically and from working in a group.
    </p>
  </DetailSection>
</Project>
